I use the "codex_targeted.R" and "segment_targeted.R" codes I got from here, with default parameters, except that I changed

finalcalli=segment_targeted(yi, yhati, sampname_qc, refi, genei, chri, lmax=length(geneindex), mode='fraction')

to

finalcalli=segment_targeted(yi, yhati, sampname_qc, refi, genei, chri, lmax=length(geneindex), mode='integer')

because I don't have cancer samples, only cases with germline mutations.

I think the problem may have something to do with only one CNV being called for that chromosome and messing up the matrix. This is because when I go through all the other results for other chromosomes, they include CODEX_frac.txt files with 0 or 2-xx amount of variant calls, but none with only one call. I'm fairly new to R and bioinformatics in general, and I don't know how to fix this error.

Best regards,

Salla

